@ 29.1.1.1.11 - Proto-Athabaskan to Han
# citation: Whimemsz, from Krauss, Michael and Victor Golla (1981), “Northern Athapaskan
# 			Languages”. Handbook of North American Indians, Vol. 6 (Subarctic), 67 – 85
	TS TŠ TŠʷ K Q > TH TS TṢ TŠ K
	# Occasional palatalization in front of high vowels
	n > (ⁿ)d / $_V:[- nasal]
	j > ʒ / $_
	a ɑ ə ʊ > æ a {ə,ë} o
	# Acquisition of vowel length, but how this occurs is not described
	Vˀ > V:[+low tone]
	# Majority of stem-final consonants lost; the only stem-finals permitted in
	# 			comtemporary Han are /t k w j r n h ʔ/, with the addition of /l/ in Dawson Han